headers {
  Accept: application/fhir+json
}

auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  # Ignitor FHIR API
  
  Manual, interactive exploration of the Ignis FHIR API.
  
  Auth: run **Ignis → Auth → Get token** once. Its post-response script stores the access
  token in the `accessToken` runtime variable, and every request inherits
  `Bearer {{accessToken}}` from the collection (`auth: inherit`). Re-run Get token
  when the token expires (you'll see 401s). `clientId` comes from the committed
  `local` environment; `clientSecret` is a Bruno **secret variable** — set it once
  in the environment editor (the dev value matches the `ignis-client` client in
  `appsettings.json`), and its value is never written to the committed files.
  
  Select the **ignis-local** environment before sending requests. Both `baseUrl` and
  `tokenUrl` target `https://localhost:5201`; disable TLS verification for the
  collection (self-signed dev cert).
}
